# --- Vendored third-party Typst packages ---
# Fetched by `backend/scripts/vendor_typst_packages.py` (pinned versions + SHA-256), run once
# after `uv sync` and again as a Docker build step. Not committed: it is third-party LGPL-3.0
# source in an otherwise proprietary first-party repository, and it is reproducible from the
# pins in that script. The running app never downloads it — see §13 and the script's docstring.
backend/app/reports/typst_packages/

# --- App data & generated output ---
# SQLite database (persistent volume in deployment; never commit real exam data)
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
backend/data/
# Rendered reports (PDF/xlsx produced at runtime, not build artifacts to track)
backend/generated/
*.generated.pdf
*.generated.xlsx

# --- Test data safety net ---
# This project handles real student personal data (Matrikelnummer, names).
# Only the known anonymized fixtures below are allowed in test_data/; any other
# PDF dropped there (e.g. a real, non-anonymized export used for local debugging)
# must never be committed.
# Each real-export fixture is allowlisted by its exact filename, deliberately: a broad
# pattern like *_TestData.pdf would silently admit the next file dropped in here, which is
# precisely the accident this rule exists to prevent. Add a line only after confirming the
# file is anonymized.
test_data/*.pdf
!test_data/ZPrf_Grundlagen_der_Informationstechnik_B_Sc_WiIng_ET_IT_WiSe_23_24_TestData.pdf
!test_data/ZPrf_Grundlagen_der_Informationstechnik_fuer_Wirtschaftsingenieurwesen_B_Sc_WiIng_ET_IT_BPO_2020_2024_SoSe_26_TestData.pdf
!test_data/*_synthetic*.pdf

